{"photo-hab-bear-claw-aspen":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-bear-claw-aspen.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: GlacierNPS, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bear_Claw_Marks_on_an_Aspen_Tree_(42501156050).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Bear claw marks: parallel scratches on smooth aspen bark where a bear climbed."},"photo-hab-bear-scat-berries":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-bear-scat-berries.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWSmidwest, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_Bear_Scat_(15274318020).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Bear scat full of berries: a berry patch nearby is in use."},"photo-hab-bear-track-front":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-bear-track-front.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: vhhammer, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Black_bear_(Ursus_americanus)_track_at_the_Hidden_Lakes_of_the_Pasayten_Wilderness..jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Black bear front track: wide pad, 5 toes in an arc."},"photo-hab-bitterbrush-leaf":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-bitterbrush-leaf.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Matt Lavin from Bozeman, Montana, USA, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Purshia_tridentata_(4036546795).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Bitterbrush: grey green dry slope shrub, tiny wedge leaves with 3 teeth. Key mule deer browse."},"photo-hab-blackberry":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-blackberry.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Thayne Tuason, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rubus_armeniacus_1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Himalayan blackberry: thorny tangles on Fraser Valley edges. Cover for deer and bears."},"photo-hab-bracken":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-bracken.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: brewbooks from near Seattle, USA, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pteridium_aquilinum_(bracken_fern)_-_Flickr_-_brewbooks.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Bracken fern: big triangle fronds on cut blocks and edges."},"photo-hab-cattail-head":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-cattail-head.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Terry.grignon, CC0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Typha_latifolia_female_and_male_spikes.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Cattail: brown sausage head, tall flat leaves. Marsh cover for ducks."},"photo-hab-ceanothus-leaf":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-ceanothus-leaf.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Thayne Tuason, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ceanothus_velutinus_var._velutinus_1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Snowbrush ceanothus: glossy sticky leaves with 3 veins from the base. Sprouts after fire. Deer browse."},"photo-hab-chokecherry":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-chokecherry.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Thayne Tuason, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prunus_virginiana_fruittwo-9-08-04.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Chokecherry: dark red to black cherries in hanging clusters. Grouse, quail and bear food."},"photo-hab-deer-pellets-fresh":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-deer-pellets-fresh.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Steve Redman ( MORA ), Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deer_scat_taken_in_2009_(b7b62065560e4e9095f9f86778c8b7b1).JPG\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Deer pellets, fresh: dark, shiny, moist. About 1 to 1.5 cm long."},"photo-hab-deer-rub":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-deer-rub.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Wasp32, CC BY 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deer_rub.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Buck rub: bark stripped from a sapling at knee to waist height, late summer to the rut."},"photo-hab-deer-track-dirt":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-deer-track-dirt.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Thayne Tuason, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Deer_tracks_near_Saddlerock_Wenatchee_Washington.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Deer track: split heart, pointed end forward, about 5 to 9 cm."},"photo-hab-dogwood-stems":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-dogwood-stems.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Matt Lavin, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cornus_sericea_-_red_osier_dogwood_-_53066633106.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Red osier dogwood: red stems, wet ground. Favourite fall and winter browse for deer and moose."},"photo-hab-douglas-fir-tree":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-douglas-fir-tree.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Matt Lavin, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pseudotsuga_menziesii_-_Douglas_fir_-_52487422990.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Douglas fir: soft flat needles, thick bark, cones with 3 pointed bracts. Winter food and thermal cover."},"photo-hab-duck-tracks":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-duck-tracks.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Ryan Hodnett, CC BY-SA 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anatidae_Footprints_-_Guelph,_Ontario_2020-04-12.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Duck track: 3 forward toes joined by webbing."},"photo-hab-elk-pellets":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-elk-pellets.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Una Smith, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elk_pellets.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Elk pellets: bigger than deer pellets, often in large piles in meadows."},"photo-hab-elk-wallow":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-elk-wallow.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Loren Lane ( MORA ), Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Elk_wallow._101981._slide_(f74312c976714e5db311641d02f847ac).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Elk wallow: muddy pit dug and rolled in by bulls in the September rut."},"photo-hab-grouse-snow-roost":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-grouse-snow-roost.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Cephas, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bonasa_umbellus_snow_hole.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Grouse snow roost: hole in soft snow with wing marks where the bird burst out."},"photo-hab-grouse-track-line":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-grouse-track-line.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: NPS, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grouse_Tracks_in_the_snow_(5547c3a5-6256-4c63-b589-8585e510ebaf).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Grouse track: 3 long toes forward, short one back, about 5 cm."},"photo-hab-huckleberry-berry":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-huckleberry-berry.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: julie from Idaho, united states, CC BY 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vaccinium_membranaceum_Fruit_and_leaves.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Black huckleberry: dark purple berry, thin oval leaves. Bear food in August and September."},"photo-hab-kinnikinnick":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-kinnikinnick.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Matt Lavin from Bozeman, Montana, USA, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arctostaphylos_uva-ursi_(5192873642).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Kinnikinnick: low evergreen mat, spoon shaped leaves, red berries. Dry open ground."},"photo-hab-moose-tracks-mud":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-moose-tracks-mud.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: USFWS Mountain-Prairie, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moose_Tracks_on_Seedskadee_National_Wildlife_Refuge_(22388750875).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Moose track: about 13 to 15 cm, more than twice a deer track."},"photo-hab-pondweed":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-pondweed.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Christian Fischer, CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PotamogetonNatans.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Floating pondweed: oval leaves on the surface. Ducks eat seeds and plants."},"photo-hab-sagebrush-bush":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-sagebrush-bush.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Z3lvs, CC0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Big_Sagebrush_(Artemisia_tridentata)_Washoe_Lake_State_Park,_Nevada_1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Big sagebrush: silver grey, strong smell. Marks dry, low winter country."},"photo-hab-salal":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-salal.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Robert Flogaus-Faust, CC BY 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gaultheria_shallon_RF.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Salal: thick oval leathery leaves, white bell flowers. Coast forest floor. Black tailed deer food."},"photo-hab-salmonberry":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-salmonberry.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Walter Siegmund (talk), CC BY-SA 3.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rubus_spectabilis_1564.JPG\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Salmonberry: raspberry like orange or red berry, wet coast ground. Spring and summer deer food."},"photo-hab-saskatoon-flowers":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-saskatoon-flowers.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Robert Flogaus-Faust, CC BY 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amelanchier_alnifolia_2_RF.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Saskatoon: oval leaves toothed on the top half, white spring flowers, purple July berries. Top deer browse."},"photo-hab-skunk-cabbage":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-skunk-cabbage.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: The Cosmonaut, CC BY-SA 2.5 CA, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lysichiton_americanus_-_Aldergrove_Regional_Park.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Western skunk cabbage: yellow hood in wet spring forest. Early spring bear food."},"photo-hab-snowberry":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-snowberry.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: NPS Photo, Public domain, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:File-Symphoricarpos_albus_-_native;-Blooms_June_-_July;_(9352ce2f-155d-4519-3e7c-5033029f6900).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Snowberry: low shrub, round leaves, white berries that last into winter."},"photo-hab-soopolallie":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-soopolallie.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Robert Flogaus-Faust, CC BY 4.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shepherdia_canadensis_2_RF.jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Soopolallie: opposite leaves, rusty undersides, red berries in July and August. Bear food."},"photo-hab-willow-shrub":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-willow-shrub.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Matt Lavin from Bozeman, Montana, USA, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Salix_bebbiana_(5002370825).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Willow: many stems, long narrow leaves, wet ground. Top moose browse."},"photo-hab-woods-rose-hips":{"front":"What is this?","photo":"<figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/hab-woods-rose-hips.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption> <span class=\"credit\">Photo: Jim Morefield from Nevada, USA, CC BY-SA 2.0, <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western_wildrose,_Rosa_woodsii_(16469499462).jpg\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">source</a></span></figcaption></figure>","back":"Wild rose: thorny stems, red hips into winter. Deer, grouse and bears eat the hips."}}